Google published two posts on 10 November 2026: one about Gemini Intelligence reaching more devices, and one about the November Pixel Drop, its periodic feature update for Pixel phones and watches. The updates were due to start that day and continue over several weeks. This explainer sets out what is listed, which phones and countries qualify, and what to check before letting an assistant act inside your apps.

*Disclosure: this post was drafted by Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic, a competitor of Google, and checked by a separate AI reviewer against the cited pages for figures, dates and wording. This is not a full human review. Stackbrook did not test any phone or feature and has no affiliate relationship with any company mentioned at the time of writing. The header image is AI-generated.*

## What Gemini Intelligence is

Gemini Intelligence is Google's name for a set of AI features on higher-end Android phones. Android Help lists multi-step app automation, proactive suggestions, Rambler voice typing, a pre-installed Gemini Notebook, writing tools, sign-to-text for American Sign Language, custom widgets and device assistance.

The same help page sets a high bar for hardware: at least 12 GB of RAM, a qualifying processor, on-device AI processing, recent media processing and passing performance benchmarks. A phone running Android is therefore not automatically eligible.

Google's blog names the Pixel 11 range, Samsung's Galaxy Z Fold8 Ultra, Z Fold8, Z Flip8 and Galaxy S26 series among the devices where the rollout began. It adds Pixel 10 phones through this update, and calls the motorola signature 27 Motorola's first such device, with US pre-orders from 19 November.

## What the November update lists

- **Multi-step tasks.** Gemini can work through jobs such as ordering food, booking a ride or reserving a table. The Pixel Drop post says this is now available in Japan, the UK and India.
- **Rambler.** Speech is turned into tidied text, with filler words such as "um" removed.
- **Proactive suggestions.** Examples include sharing your arrival time with a tap. The footnote requires a Pixel 10 or newer (not the 10a), the Gemini app and setup, and limits the feature to select countries and languages and to users aged 18 or over.
- **Custom widgets.** You describe a widget, such as a spending tracker or a holiday countdown, and Gemini builds it.
- **Conversation summaries.** The post says they are now available in German, French, Spanish, Italian, Hindi and Traditional Chinese.
- **Call Screen.** On Pixel 11 phones in the US, Gemini can ask unknown callers why they are calling and show a live transcript.
- **Device assistance.** The Gemini Intelligence post gives examples such as freeing up space or checking which apps can see your location, on select devices running Android 17 or later.

The Pixel Drop also includes smaller items. HiLight can glow for favourite contacts' messages on the Pixel 11 Pro, Pro XL and Pro Fold. Google also announced the Pixel Tag tracker, available from 11 November at $29.99 for one or $99.99 for four. For Pixel search, the post body says Pixel 6 and newer while its footnote says Pixel 6a and newer. Proactive suggestions are promised for Pixel Watch 4 later. Separately, the Gemini Intelligence post says proactive suggestions are coming soon to Android Auto.

